    "tpa_score_new": "<table>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>評分規則說明</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div><strong>9 drafts for 3 topics (60 %)</strong></div>\n\n\t\t\t<ul>\n\t\t\t\t<li>Your final version on topic I due&nbsp;<strong>Week 6</strong></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li>Your final version on topic II due&nbsp;<strong>Week 9</strong></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li>Your final version on topic III due&nbsp;<strong>Week 15</strong></li>\n\t\t\t\t<li><strong>P</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>r</strong><strong>t</strong><strong>f</strong><strong>ol</strong><strong>i</strong><strong>o:</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>At the&nbsp;</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>nd of</strong><strong>&nbsp;eac</strong><strong>h&nbsp;</strong><strong>s</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>mest</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>r</strong><strong>, by&nbsp;week 17,&nbsp;</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>v</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>r</strong><strong>y</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>student shou</strong><strong>l</strong><strong>d h</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>nd in</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>c</strong><strong>omp</strong><strong>l</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>te port</strong><strong>f</strong><strong>ol</strong><strong>i</strong><strong>o</strong><strong>&nbsp;of the</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>d</strong><strong>r</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>f</strong><strong>ts of&nbsp;</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>ll</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>w</strong><strong>r</strong><strong>i</strong><strong>t</strong><strong>ing</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>modes</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>w</strong><strong>i</strong><strong>t</strong><strong>h a</strong><strong>&nbsp;c</strong><strong>ov</strong><strong>e</strong><strong>r page</strong><strong>&nbsp;a</strong><strong>nd</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>a</strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>ta</strong><strong>b</strong><strong>le of&nbsp;</strong><strong>c</strong><strong>ontents.</strong></li>\n\t\t\t</ul>\n\n\t\t\t<div><strong>Peer-review (20%)</strong></div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>You will be divided into four or five co-working groups to review each others writing as a team. You will be graded on how well you have integrated feedback from your classmates as well as the elements we studied in class into you rewrite. &nbsp;</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div><strong>In-class participation and attendance (20%)</strong></div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>＊The course plan may be adjusted as needed throughout the semester＊</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n",
    "tpa_score_new_en": null,
    "course_pol": "Personal feedback directly from me is on offer at any time throughout the semester. \nIf you would like comments from me on anything that you write, that you provide me with a hard copy (paper version) of your writing.\nNo feedback will will be given by me on any writing sent via email or uploaded online. \nThis goes for your final dossier as well. If you would like feedback from me, please give me a paper version of your dossier.\nRecording, filming, and photography are prohibited in class without prior consent.\n\n＊The course plan may be adjusted as needed throughout the semester＊",
    "course_pol_en": "評分規則說明\n9 drafts for 3 topics (60 %)\nYour final version on topic I due Week 6\nYour final version on topic II due Week 9\nYour final version on topic III due Week 15\nPortfolio: At the end of each semester, on week 17-18, every student should hand in a complete portfolio of the drafts of all writing modes with a cover page and a table of contents.\nPeer-review (20%)\nYou will be divided into four or five co-working groups to review each others writing as a team. You will be graded on how well you have integrated feedback from your classmates as well as the elements we studied in class into you rewrite.  \nIn-class participation and attendance (20%)\n \n＊The course plan may be adjusted as needed throughout the semester＊",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": "<table>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<th>綜合說明</th>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div><strong>Every writing assignment you turn in counts for 10% of your grade</strong>, so it is very important to turn in&nbsp;<strong>each piece on time</strong>. You must&nbsp;<strong>bring a printed or written version</strong>&nbsp;of every draft to class, so I can give you feedback.</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>If you use AI, you must&nbsp;<strong>explain how you used it</strong>&mdash;or don&rsquo;t use it at all.</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div><strong>＊</strong><strong>Students will be expected to finish the first draft of the three chosen topics in class.</strong></div>\n\n\t\t\t<div><strong>＊</strong><strong>The peer-review method will be applied in class. &nbsp;</strong></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n",
    "ais_meno_en": "<table>\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div><strong>Every writing assignment you turn in counts for 10% of your grade</strong>, so it is very important to turn in&nbsp;<strong>each piece on time</strong>. You must&nbsp;<strong>bring a printed or written version</strong>&nbsp;of every draft to class, so I can give you feedback.</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>If you use AI, you must&nbsp;<strong>explain how you used it</strong>&mdash;or don&rsquo;t use it at all.</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>\n\t\t\t<div><strong>＊</strong><strong>Students will be expected to finish the first draft of the three chosen topics in class.</strong></div>\n\n\t\t\t<div><strong>＊</strong><strong>The peer-review method will be applied in class. &nbsp;</strong></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n",
